plumbing: revlist, Document which objects Objects excludes

The `Objects` doc said only that commits reachable from haves are
excluded, which leaves open how its object set compares with
`git rev-list --objects`. It differs on purpose: the built-in walk
excludes every tree and blob reachable from each have commit's tree,
as well as from the edge commits' trees, while Git marks only the edge
commits' trees uninteresting (`mark_edges_uninteresting` in Git's
`list-objects.c`). go-git can therefore return fewer objects than Git,
but none that a client with those haves lacks, since the haves' full
trees are already on the client.

State this in the doc so storers and callers comparing against Git
know the difference is intended. No behaviour changes.

